{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.85,"content_digest":"6599e8937e0577971a67a7964f3f33a62ccf7ae02dba7e725cefd379ffff4f60","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:00:24+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"38d221019a9d4238d00314cc5272493e665eb9955dd9f3899263d7e8c0cab43e","input_tokens":5705,"latency_ms":38090,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"87f086c3f2b815570f83b4c4cfb87355eeb2aa62b7da6c14d27608af48a3623a","output_tokens":2740,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:73bd9de6f3a1d5e868ee8ad4","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:unsupervised-identifiability","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QB99J9QD4MGQS73QP5B6Y7","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that latent factors are not identifiable from observations alone without additional constraints. The new principle is a specialized instance in the AI-evaluation setting: finite evaluation-aware behavioral evidence can be consistent with multiple latent hypotheses, so latent alignment is not uniquely identified. Both concern observational underdetermination of latent structure.","relation_type":"generalizes","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:00:24+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
